WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:07.580
Hi guys, my name is Griffin and I was born in and still am in Indianapolis, Indiana.
大家好，我叫格里芬，我出生在印第安纳州印第安纳波利斯，现在也住在那。

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:17.579
When how my brother came out, my mom came to the responsible conclusion that maybe I wasn't quite ready for this show since I was only 5 years old.
当我的兄弟出柜时，我妈妈做出了一个负责任的决定，鉴于我当时只有5岁，也许我还没准备好观看这部剧。

00:00:17.579 --> 00:00:24.579
When I first watched the show, I was 13 years old or about the same age that Ted's kids were in the future Ted scenes.
当我第一次看这部剧时，我13岁，差不多和泰德未来场景里他的孩子们同龄。

00:00:24.579 --> 00:00:30.579
I instantly fell in love with the dynamics between the characters and all the hidden messages and themes put into single episode stories.
我一眼就爱上了角色之间的化学反应，以及融入到单集故事中的所有隐藏信息和主题。

00:00:30.579 --> 00:00:32.089
stories and season-long arcs.
各种故事和贯穿全季的故事线。

00:00:32.089 --> 00:00:44.218
I grew lacking a father figure in a weird way you're writing filled that void as if it was talking to me as one of the kids on the couch telling me that you're gonna try very hard, you're gonna win a lot, and you're gonna lose a lot.
我成长过程中缺乏父爱，从某种奇怪的角度来说，你们的剧本填补了这一空白，就好像它在跟我说话，就像坐在沙发上的其中一个孩子一样，告诉我你会非常努力，你会赢很多次，也会输很多次。

00:00:44.218 --> 00:00:50.726
In the end you'll be thankful for all the experiences you've had both good and bad because it got you to where you are today.
最后，你会感谢你所经历的一切，无论是好的还是坏的，因为正是这些经历造就了今天的你。

00:00:50.726 --> 00:01:00.564
I have long desired to live in the city culture seen in this show and at the time of recording this I'm glad to say that I will be moving out of my home town to San Francisco in three days.
我一直渴望体验这部剧里展现的都市文化，而在录制这期节目的时候，我很高兴地说，我将在三天后离开家乡，搬到旧金山。

00:01:00.564 --> 00:01:10.819
This show gave me the confidence to do things that were ambitious instead of things that were practical and it taught me valuable lessons that I honestly don't know where else I would have learned.
这部剧给了我信心去做有抱负的事情，而不是只做务实的事情，它教给我宝贵的道理，说实话，我不知道自己还能从哪里学到这些。

00:01:10.819 --> 00:01:16.896
Thank you guys so much for pouring your hearts and souls into the writing of these characters and the world around them.
非常感谢你们倾注心血创作这些角色以及他们周围的世界。

00:01:16.896 --> 00:01:20.340
Your writing was and still is my anchor for understanding the world.
你们的剧本过去是、现在仍然是我理解这个世界的精神锚点。

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:44.079
Well hello and welcome to another episode of How We Made Your Mother.
大家好，欢迎收看新一期的《我们是如何创造你母亲的》。

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:46.115
I am here with my friend Craig Thomas.
我是主持人，我的朋友克雷格·托马斯也在场。

00:01:46.115 --> 00:01:46.615
Hi Craig.
嗨，克雷格。

00:01:46.615 --> 00:01:47.115
Hey Josh.
嘿，乔希。

00:01:47.079 --> 00:01:51.079
We're talking about the TV show we made together from 2005 to 2014.
我们在聊我们从2005年到2014年一起制作的电视剧。

00:01:51.079 --> 00:01:52.079
It was called How I Met Your Mother.
它叫《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:54.439
We're going back through every episode.
我们要回顾每一集。

00:01:54.439 --> 00:01:58.239
We're rewatching, we're rewinding, we're reconsidering.
我们重温，我们倒带，我们重新思考。

00:01:58.239 --> 00:02:00.640
We're liking what we see for the most part.
总的来说，我们很喜欢我们看到的内容。

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:08.000
I gotta say that I am delighted, one, because we have one of the great, how I met your mother, guest stars with us today.
我必须说，我感到非常高兴，首先，因为我们今天迎来了《老爸老妈浪漫史》中最伟大的客串明星之一。

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:15.080
And while the theme song was playing, which is my song, New York City, he was bobbing his head along and delighting it.
刚才主题曲播放的时候——那是我的歌《纽约市》——他一直跟着点头，听得津津有味。

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.759
And he said, Josh, is this you?
然后他说：“乔希，这是你唱的吗？”

00:02:16.759 --> 00:02:18.639
And I said, yeah, and he seemed to approve.
我说：“是的，”他似乎很认可。

00:02:18.639 --> 00:02:24.120
So I'm delighted that Wayne Brady also got the note that we like to have all the guests bearded.
所以我很高兴韦恩·布莱迪也注意到我们喜欢所有嘉宾都留胡子这一点。

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.879
He showed up with the beard.
他带着胡子来了。

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:29.800
Please give the warmest, Twymium welcome to Wayne Brady.
请用最热烈的双关语欢迎韦恩·布莱迪。

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:30.639
Hey, Wayne.
嘿，韦恩。

00:02:30.639 --> 00:02:32.280
Yes, hey, man.
嘿，老兄。

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.639
Hey, great job on the song.
嘿，这首歌唱得真棒。

00:02:33.639 --> 00:02:34.479
Thanks, man.
谢谢，老兄。

00:02:34.479 --> 00:02:35.319
That was great.
太棒了。

00:02:35.319 --> 00:02:36.159
Thank you.
谢谢。

00:02:36.159 --> 00:02:45.439
Because immediately I recognized your voice, which was part of being, you know, I'm not gonna say a good singer or it's part of having a voice that you affect folks.
因为我立刻就认出了你的声音，这可以说是……你知道的，我不是说他是个优秀的歌手，但这是一种能触动人们内心的嗓音。

00:02:45.439 --> 00:02:50.120
I went, oh, that's your voice and I know your voice and I really liked it.
我当时想：“哦，那是你的声音，我认得你的声音，我真的很喜欢。”

00:02:50.120 --> 00:03:03.800
Well, have you noticed that some singers, their speaking voice and singing voice are very similar and other people, I know this great singer in Nashville, Audrey Asad, her speaking voice gives you no indication about how glorious her singing voice is.
那么，你有没有发现有些歌手，他们的说话声音和唱歌声音非常相似，而另我知道纳什维尔有一位伟大的歌手，奥黛丽·阿萨德，她的说话声音根本无法让人猜出她唱歌的声音有多么辉煌。

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:04.639
Do you know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

00:03:04.639 --> 00:03:05.479
There could be that difference.
可能会有这种差异。

00:03:05.479 --> 00:03:07.360
They are vocal catfishes.
他们是声音上的“姜太公钓鱼”（愿者上钩，指声音伪装者/反差萌）。

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:08.199
Yes.
没错。

00:03:08.199 --> 00:03:09.680
They absolutely have a catfish.
他们绝对是个“声音诈骗犯”。

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:11.520
You know who really does that?
你知道谁经常这样吗？

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:12.639
British artists.
英国艺术家。

00:03:12.639 --> 00:03:13.479
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

00:03:13.479 --> 00:03:14.319
Oh, yeah, all the time.
哦，是的，总是这样。

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:18.520
Oh, I really don't, and then they singing, oh, because I'm from the hoodish.
哦，我真的不知道，然后他们一唱歌，“哦，因为我来自街头呢。”

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:21.520
It's like, what?
就好像，什么？

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:23.039
I remember that beetle song.
我记得那首披头士的歌。

00:03:23.039 --> 00:03:28.520
I love that you're still in character coining new phrases, bringing the James energy.
我喜欢你依然保持着角色的状态，创造新的短语，带来詹姆斯的能量。

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:29.360
That's what I do.
这就是我的风格。

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:30.800
I love it, vocal catfish.
我太喜欢了，“声音诈骗犯”。

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:34.879
Well, Wayne, we're really so happy to have you on the show.
好吧，韦恩，我们真的非常高兴你能来节目。

00:03:34.879 --> 00:03:37.280
But remind us, how many episodes did you do?
不过提醒我们一下，你演了多少集？

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.159
Do you even know how many episodes you're on?
你甚至知道你演了多少集吗？

00:03:39.159 --> 00:03:48.039
I don't remember, because it seemed like a lot, but like my daughter, it was like six, and it was something like that spread across a bunch of years.
我不记得了，因为感觉挺多的，但就像我女儿说的，大概有六集，差不多就是跨越了好几年的那种数量。

00:03:48.039 --> 00:03:55.960
This is the first one we're talking about the episode, Single Stamina, where we meet you six to eight, something like that, a couple of them were very small appearances, a couple of them were bigger.
这是我们讨论的第一集，单身耐力，我们在那一集里遇到了你，6到8集，诸如此类，其中有几集只是客串了一下，有几集戏份比较多。

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:57.960
This is a great episode, Single Stamina.
这一集太棒了，《单身耐力》。

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.719
I had not watched this episode in years.
我已经好几年没看过这一集了。

00:04:00.719 --> 00:04:02.759
You are great in this, my friend.
老朋友，你在里面表现得太棒了。

00:04:02.759 --> 00:04:06.800
It is such, you just burst in and steal the show.
简直是……你一出场就惊艳全场，抢尽了风头。

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:07.879
It is so great.
真的太棒了。

00:04:07.879 --> 00:04:12.599
Before we dive in, can we just do our, Alec, tell us when this episode aired?
在我们深入探讨之前，亚历克，能告诉我们这一集是什么时候播出的吗？

00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:17.040
So Single Stamina aired on November 27th, 2006.
《单身耐力》于2006年11月27日播出。

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:25.120
And I just want to say that if chat GPT is to be believed, chat GPT believes that you were on 13 episodes of How I Met Your Mother.
我只想说，如果相信ChatGPT的话，ChatGPT认为你演了13集《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:28.519
13, okay, then that makes sense.
13集，好吧，那倒说得通。

00:04:28.519 --> 00:04:33.360
No, but 13 makes sense because I remember being there more.
不，13集说得通，因为我记得我在那里的时间更多。

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:34.680
That's it.
就是这样。

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.519
Oh, I thought Bob did once.
哦，我还以为鲍勃只演过一次。

00:04:36.519 --> 00:04:37.360
Yeah.
对。

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.040
Yeah, that's great.
对，太棒了。

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:44.680
Single Stamina was one of the coolest experiences from beginning to end.
《单身耐力》从头到尾都是最酷的经历之一。

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:54.860
And I just did an interview where I was giving you guys props because to me to get an offer, like, hey, you know the show, how I met your mother.
我刚做了一个采访，在采访中我还在夸你们，因为对我来说，能接到这样的邀约，比如：“嘿，你知道《老爸老妈浪漫史》这部剧吗？”

00:04:54.860 --> 00:05:00.259
And I think you guys were just in your second season, but at that point, so I'd seen the first season.
我想你们当时刚进入第二季，但那时我已经看过第一季了。

00:05:00.259 --> 00:05:01.339
Of course, I know Neil.
当然，我认识尼尔。

00:05:01.339 --> 00:05:02.740
I was like, oh my God, the show is great.
我当时想：“哦天哪，这剧太棒了。”

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.100
And it introduced me to you, Josh.
它让我认识了你，乔希。

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:05.379
And I was like, this is great.
我当时觉得：“太棒了。”

00:05:05.379 --> 00:05:08.379
Oh, they want me on the show.
“哦，他们想让我上节目。”

00:05:08.379 --> 00:05:11.939
Yeah, they want you to play Neil's brother.
“对，他们想让你演尼尔的兄弟。”

00:05:11.939 --> 00:05:15.060
And immediately I went, okay, he's gay.
我立刻就想：“好吧，他是同性恋。”

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:21.819
I went, oh, so when else do you get to play Neil Patrick Harris's gay black brother?
我想：“哦，还有什么时候能有机会扮演尼尔·帕特里克·哈里斯的同性恋黑人兄弟呢？”

00:05:21.819 --> 00:05:23.379
This is it, this was your one shot.
就是这次，这是你唯一的机会。

00:05:23.379 --> 00:05:25.459
You had to say yes if you wanted to do that.
如果你想演的话，你必须答应。

00:05:25.459 --> 00:05:27.779
Not many actors get this chance.
没多少演员能有这个机会。

00:05:27.779 --> 00:05:30.180
This was the shot and it was really cool.
这就是那个机会，真的很酷。

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:42.579
And the fact that you wrapped up and resolved his whole thing with dads later, it was one of the coolest casting slash writing choices that I've seen in sitcoms.
而且你们后来圆满解决了父亲的问题，这是我在情景喜剧中见过的最酷的选角兼编剧选择之一。

00:05:42.579 --> 00:05:50.779
It was brave without being, being, hey, look what we're doing, because you put the funny first, but you also had the heart.
它很勇敢，但又不会刻意表现“嘿，看我们在做什么”，因为你们把搞笑放在首位，但同时也充满了温情。

00:05:50.779 --> 00:05:54.060
So I'm always blessed that I got to do that.
所以我一直很庆幸自己能参与其中。

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:55.819
Oh, man, we were so lucky to have you.
天哪，我们能请到你真是太幸运了。

00:05:55.819 --> 00:05:59.500
You kind of just answered my question, which was we were a second season show.
你其实已经回答了我的问题，那就是我们当时是一部第二季的剧。

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:00.579
We were not a big hit.
我们当时并不是什么大热剧。

00:06:00.579 --> 00:06:01.939
We asked Brian Cranston this too.
我们问过布莱恩·克兰斯顿这个问题。

00:06:01.939 --> 00:06:04.819
He was an episode a couple before this one, the one you're in.
他在你出演的那一集之前几集也客串过。

00:06:04.819 --> 00:06:09.620
And our question to him that I kind of would say to you too is, why did you do this?
我们当时问他的问题，其实我也想问你：你当时为什么要接？

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:20.220
I like, why this is the weirdest character, the weirdest offer, we were not a hit show, you maybe saw a little bit of season one, maybe, like, maybe you saw all of season one, I don't know, but there wasn't a lot of season one.
我想，为什么这是最奇怪的角色，最奇怪的邀约，我们不是一部大热剧，你可能看过一点第一季，也许吧，也许你看完了第一季，我不知道，但当时第一季也没播多少。

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:22.060
You all seemed well, I'm very honored that you did.
你们看起来都挺好，我很荣幸你们接了。

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:23.459
Because it was fresh.
因为这部剧很有新意。

00:06:23.459 --> 00:06:28.660
So I knew A, that it was the ground floor of something great, like friends.
所以我知道第一，这是一部伟大作品的基石，就像《老友记》一样。

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:33.860
And then B, the fact that because you weren't a big hit yet, you wrote what you wanted to.
第二，正因为你们当时还不是大热门，所以你们想写什么就写什么。

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:38.220
You wrote funny versus trying to do whatever the next guy was doing.
你们写的是喜剧，而不是去模仿别人在做什么。

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:43.759
And I, and I think in comedy, you always wanna be aligned with that.
而且我，我觉得在喜剧里，你总是想和那种感觉保持一致。

00:06:43.759 --> 00:06:46.639
So I was really happy to get that call.
所以我接到那个电话时真的很高兴。

00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:53.639
You know, Craig, I know you seem to think that actors are doing a favor in those for certain reasons by being on the show.
你知道，克雷格，我知道你似乎觉得演员出于某些原因去客串那些节目是在帮剧组的忙。

00:06:53.639 --> 00:06:54.720
I definitely do, I guess.
我确实这么觉得，我猜吧。

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:57.959
We're getting paid to act, which we always enjoy, you know.
我们演戏是有片酬的，而且我们一直很享受演戏，你知道的。

00:06:57.959 --> 00:07:07.560
And two, if you see enough, like a new show that's on that is kind of like delightful and weird and new, they send you an offer, you read the script, you're like, hey, this is a great part.
第二，如果你看到足够多的新剧，那种既讨喜、古怪又新鲜的剧，他们给你发了邀约，你看了剧本，就会觉得，嘿，这是一个很棒的角色。

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:09.720
you're mostly gonna do it if you're available.
如果你刚好有档期，你多半就会接。

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:10.560
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:17.540
It's not like great opportunities are falling from the trees of like new young cool shows that are, you know what I mean?
那些很棒的机会又不是从树上掉下来的，那种全新的、年轻的、很酷的剧，你知道我的意思吗？

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:28.160
I think you underestimate and undersell that even though the show wasn't a ratings juggernaut, it was still being noticed and watched and people were talking about it.
我觉得你低估并贬低了一点，那就是尽管这部剧当时并不是收视巨无霸，但它依然受到了关注和观看，人们也一直在讨论它。

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:29.000
Absolutely.
绝对是的。

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:33.439
I just remember feeling at the time, it felt like such a get.
我只记得当时的感觉，能请到你就像是捡到宝一样。

00:07:33.439 --> 00:07:34.720
We were all such fans of yours.
我们所有人都是你的超级粉丝。

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.199
Everyone in the writers who loved you, everybody loves you.
编剧室里的每个人都超喜欢你，所有人都爱你。

00:07:37.199 --> 00:07:43.519
Everyone in the writer's room had been obsessed with you on the Chappelle show appearance where you came into that show and stole that whole episode.
编剧室里的每一个人都对你在《查佩尔秀》里的客串着迷不已，你一出场就把整集都给盘活了。

00:07:43.519 --> 00:07:46.839
And we had all watched that 75,000 times in the writer's room.
我们在编剧室里把那一集看过了整整七万五千遍。

00:07:46.839 --> 00:07:48.959
So we were all starstruck with you coming in.
所以你一来，我们所有人都有点像见到偶像一样肃然起敬。

00:07:48.959 --> 00:07:53.240
And I definitely had that feeling early on, like, this guy's doing us a real favor here.
我早期确实有那种感觉，觉得“这家伙真的是在帮我们一个大忙”。

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:54.279
Like, same with Cranston.
就像对克兰斯顿一样。

00:07:54.279 --> 00:07:56.279
I was like, how are they coming to do this for us?
当时我就想，他们怎么会愿意来为我们演这个？

00:07:56.279 --> 00:07:57.959
Josh is absolutely right.
乔希完全说得对。

00:07:57.959 --> 00:08:01.079
Don't get it twisted, no matter who you are as the actor.
别搞错了，不管你作为演员多大牌。

00:08:01.079 --> 00:08:02.680
If there's something cool.
如果有很酷的东西。

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:03.519
Yeah, you wanna do it.
是的，你会想演。

00:08:03.519 --> 00:08:05.399
You wanna be part of something cool.
你会想成为酷炫事物的一部分。

00:08:05.399 --> 00:08:06.959
You definitely wanna do it.
你绝对会想去演的。

00:08:06.959 --> 00:08:13.199
Yeah, yeah, it's also cool to be in on the ground floor if something like, don't wait until it's like, help make it a hit.
对，对，能够在某个事物刚起步时就参与其中也很酷，而不是等到它火了才加入——去帮它成为一部热门剧。

00:08:13.199 --> 00:08:14.040
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:23.319
Like, lend your whatever power you have to kind of burnish the thing and be a part of something like before, you know, help turn it into what it became.
就像是，贡献你拥有的任何影响力去给它增光添彩，在它成形之前就成为其中的一部分，你知道的，帮它变成后来那个样子。

00:08:23.319 --> 00:08:25.120
And I think you did that for us.
我觉得你为我们做到了这一点。

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:33.879
Real quick, Craig, just so people watching along are people who maybe haven't seen the episode in a while, just give us your kind of armchair summary of what this episode was.
克雷格，简单说一下，为了让正在看节目的观众，或者可能有一段时间没看这一集的人有个概念，能不能给我们大致总结一下这一集讲的是什么？

00:08:33.879 --> 00:08:43.399
Yeah, this is where Robin meets Barney's brother and everybody else knows that Barney's brother is gay and black, except Robin.
好的，这一集讲的是罗宾遇到了巴尼的弟弟，除了罗宾以外，所有人都知道巴尼的弟弟是个又黑又gay的同性恋。

00:08:43.399 --> 00:08:49.200
And he comes to town and comes bursting through the door and Robin's like, oh, I did not know that.
他来到城里，砰地一声撞开大门，罗宾当时就惊了：“哦，我完全不知道这事。”

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:56.320
And basically comes in and takes them all out on the town at this moment where everybody has coupled up except Barney.
基本上他一登场，就把大家全都带出去嗨皮了，当时除了巴尼之外，大家都已经成双成对。

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:12.039
It's really an episode about Barney's loneliness and vulnerability and the fact that the one person he still feels so connected to is his brother, But the big reveal along the way is that his brother has committed the ultimate cardinal sin according to Barney, which is falling in love and getting in a couple when he's engaged.
这其实是一集关于巴尼的孤独感和脆弱感的剧，他唯一还觉得有着紧密联系的人就是他的弟弟，但随之而来的最大反转是，他的弟弟犯了巴尼眼中的终极大忌——那就是在订婚后坠入爱河并步入了两人世界。

00:09:12.039 --> 00:09:19.120
And so there's this huge reveal and Barney feels so betrayed and Barney has to learn to accept that his brother is going to get married.
所以这里有一个巨大的反转，巴尼感到自己遭到了背叛，而巴尼不得不学会接受他的弟弟要结婚的事实。

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:20.679
The worst thing that could happen, anybody.
这对任何人来说都是可能发生的最糟糕的事情。

00:09:20.679 --> 00:09:28.879
I would say the central joke of the episode is that except for being black and being gay, he is like Barney in every other way.
我想这一集的核心笑话是，除了肤色和性取向不同之外，他在其他任何方面都跟巴尼一模一样。

00:09:28.879 --> 00:09:30.120
And he was so gross.
而且他太恶心了（注：原文口误或语气词，此处意指两人性格如出一辙的疯狂）。

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:33.600
Barney considers, I think, James to be his lifelong wingman.
巴尼认为，詹姆斯可以说是他一辈子的僚机。

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:40.399
Like if Ted desserts him, Marshall desserts him, he will always have James to roll through life and roll through the clubs with.
就像泰德抛弃了他、马歇尔抛弃了他，他身边的詹姆斯也永远不会变，能陪他一起闯荡生活、混迹各大夜店。

00:09:40.399 --> 00:09:50.409
And I wrote you this little day to send you in New York City.
我为你写了这段小开场白，好在纽约市迎接你。

00:09:50.409 --> 00:10:01.029
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

00:10:01.029 --> 00:10:02.990
And now, back to the show.
欢迎回到节目。

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:05.350
Yeah, I loved your guys' connection in that episode, Wayne.
韦恩，我真的很喜欢你们俩在那一集里的化学反应。

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:13.350
And another thing that was funny about how young our series was, is we were having you come in and be like, Okay, you're gonna be gay black Barney, go.
关于我们当时的剧有多年轻，还有一件很有趣的事，就是我们当时让你来演，然后说：“好吧，你要演一个同性恋黑人巴尼，开始吧。”

00:10:13.350 --> 00:10:15.629
And there was only one season of Barney.
当时巴尼这个角色才播了一季。

00:10:15.629 --> 00:10:18.889
It's not like you were coming in season eight to be like, yeah, I know what the Barney thing is.
并不是说你在第八季才来，好像你对巴尼已经很了解一样。

00:10:18.889 --> 00:10:24.350
There wasn't that much Barney, but you had to come in and be like, revealed that you had taught Barney so much.
那时候没多少巴尼的背景，但你一上来就得表现得好像你教了巴尼很多东西一样。

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:25.669
You were his big brother.
你是他的大哥。

00:10:25.669 --> 00:10:33.629
You had to sort of out Barney Barney, but in your own completely different way, what did that feel like coming in and having to hit all of those notes?
你某种程度上必须比巴尼更“巴尼”，但又要用你自己完全不同的方式，当你走进来必须完美呈现所有这些细节时，你是什么感觉？

00:10:33.629 --> 00:10:47.190
It was one of those things that, because luckily, like I said, I'd watch the show, but rarely do you get the opportunity that someone says, come in and do something very specific to what the other actor's doing.
这是那种……因为幸运的是，就像我说的，我看过这部剧，但你很少有机会能听到别人说：“进来吧，演一个跟另一个演员的表演高度契合的角色。”

00:10:47.190 --> 00:11:04.389
So in a way, the pressure was off because I knew what the legend dairy thing was, but also now I have to also be my, that I've got to make James his own guy so that you guys know what he is.
所以在某种程度上，压力反而减轻了，因为我知道传奇角色的风格是什么样的，但同时我也必须塑造出詹姆斯自己的特色，让你们知道他是个什么样的人。

00:11:04.389 --> 00:11:06.389
So that was cool.
所以这很酷。

00:11:06.389 --> 00:11:14.389
And I think, I definitely think, I mean, like not to blow smoke, but like you guys, the writing, it was there.
而且我觉得，绝对是的，不是为了拍马屁，而是你们的剧本，底子就在那里。

00:11:14.389 --> 00:11:18.470
And then you just were able to take it and go to the other place with it.
然后你们能够直接拿来，并把它带到一个更高的境界。

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:23.190
And then working with Neil was so great because I already knew Neil and we'd worked together.
而且和尼尔合作太棒了，因为我本来就认识尼尔，我们以前合作过。

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:24.710
So we had a report.
所以我们之间很有默契。

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:25.549
What had you done?
你们之前合作过什么？

00:11:25.549 --> 00:11:26.389
I was gonna ask you that, yeah?
我正想问你呢，对吧？

00:11:26.389 --> 00:11:28.070
I don't remember what you had done.
我不记得你以前做过什么了。

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:39.269
I'd been a fan of Neil's and I've done like, you know, those specials when you get together and Jerry Lewis telethon.
我一直是尼尔的粉丝，我做过那种……你知道的，大家聚在一起的特别节目，还有杰瑞·刘易斯慈善募捐晚会。

00:11:39.269 --> 00:11:43.830
Yes, it was like those things, not the actual telethon, but something like that.
对，就是那种活动，不是真正的募捐晚会，但类似这种。

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:48.389
But I did something with him and we crossed paths and we just had a great time talking.
我和他一起做过节目，我们有过交集，聊天聊得很开心。

00:11:48.389 --> 00:11:52.710
So I felt no weirdness when we met.
所以当我们见面时，我一点也没有觉得尴尬。

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:55.269
It was so welcoming and the ramp was there.
气氛非常融洽，入戏也很顺利。

00:11:55.269 --> 00:11:59.190
I said, all right, well, let me just do what I do and see if you guys like it.
我说，好吧，那我就做我擅长的事，看看你们喜不喜欢。

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:04.710
And I remember loving that first scene with the suit and being able to come in and talk about the suit.
我记得我很喜欢和他在西装店的那场戏，能够走进去谈论西装。

00:12:04.710 --> 00:12:07.549
and he's like, hey, the high five, is that back up?
然后他说：“嘿，击掌这个动作，现在又流行回来了吗？”

00:12:07.549 --> 00:12:08.389
And that whole thing.
还有整段那种互动。

00:12:08.389 --> 00:12:10.870
It was so cool.
太酷了。

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:14.350
You come into that scene, like the Tasmanian devil from Looney Tunes.
你走进那个场景时，就像《乐一通》里的塔斯马尼亚恶魔一样。

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:17.509
You burst into that apartment and just take it over.
你冲进那个公寓，直接反客为主。

00:12:17.509 --> 00:12:18.950
It is so great.
这真的太棒了。

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:21.629
And that like Wyoming speech, we're all going out.
还有那个关于怀俄明的演讲，我们要一起出去玩。

00:12:21.629 --> 00:12:27.830
I forget if that's a later scene, but you give the speech about like people in Wyoming, we need to do this for people and basements in Wyoming.
我忘了那是后面的戏还是哪场，但你发表了一段演讲，大概是关于怀俄明州的人，我们需要为怀俄明州地下室里的人们做点什么。

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:30.830
We're young, we're alive, we're in New York City, get out here.
我们年轻，我们充满生机，我们在纽约市，快出来吧。

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:33.669
That is a speech, that could be like an audition speech.
那真是一段台词，简直可以当作试镜的台词了。

00:12:33.669 --> 00:12:34.950
That was like a thing of beauty.
那简直是个艺术品。

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:35.429
What do you do?
你当时是怎么演的？

00:12:35.429 --> 00:12:36.429
It was so much fun.
真的太有趣了。

00:12:36.429 --> 00:12:38.629
That is an acceptable piece, what you did there.
你当时在那里表现得无懈可击。

00:12:38.629 --> 00:12:45.789
Wayne, did you do any sort of like how much fidelity did you want to have to Neil's Barney?
韦恩，你当时在表演时是怎么处理的？你对尼尔饰演的巴尼模仿或契合度有多少要求？

00:12:45.789 --> 00:12:46.950
Like, did you study that?
比如，你有去研究过吗？

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:51.269
Or did you say, OK, I know the basic outlines of it and I'm going to make it my own?
还是说你觉得，“好吧，我知道他的大致轮廓，我要演出我自己的风格”？

00:12:51.269 --> 00:13:00.070
Yes, I want it to be because I realized that if I was his older brother and he got some of his game for me, but we shouldn't be exactly alike.
是的，我希望是后者，因为我意识到如果我是他的大哥，他的一些把妹绝招是从我这学来的，但我们不应该完全一模一样。

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:05.830
So I just wanted, so I just needed to play the broad strokes, especially that where it comes from.
所以我只是希望，我只需要抓住大致的轮廓，尤其是那些招式的来源。

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:06.850
Oh, yeah, you know, we do this.
哦，对，你知道的，我们这样做。

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:11.929
We do that, but I felt that I should have a little more maturity than he did.
我们那样做，但我感觉我应该比他更有成熟稳重一点。

00:13:12.309 --> 00:13:14.470
So I wanted to be a little more grounded.
所以我希望角色能更接地气一些。

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:17.570
And so I did think about that as the scenes, scenes went on.
所以在拍摄一场接一场的戏时，我的确考虑了这一点。

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:25.509
And like I said, so much of it was on the paper that even when, when we get to the point later, he's a little betrayed by, by, hey, but we're doing this thing.
就像我说的，很大一部分内容都已经在剧本上了，甚至当我们拍到后面那个情节时，他对巴尼感到有点背叛，因为“嘿，我们在做这事呢”。

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:28.870
He needed to feel like, yeah, I used to do that.
他需要表现得像是：“没错，我以前也这么干过。”

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:29.650
That's great.
这太棒了。

00:13:29.650 --> 00:13:39.012
And I felt that that was something that I could bring is a little that that grounding big big brother energy where Neil just had to be at a 10 all the time.
我觉得我能带给角色的东西就是那种接地气的大哥气场，而尼尔则需要随时保持在亢奋的十级状态。

00:13:39.012 --> 00:13:51.434
Yeah, you know it's occurring to me that that a lot of how I met your mother episodes are microcosms of the macrocosm and how I met your mother you could make an argument the entire show is about growing up.
是的，我突然意识到，《老爸老妈浪漫史》的很多单集其实都是整部剧宏大主题的缩影，你完全可以说整部剧讲的就是关于成长的故事。

00:13:51.434 --> 00:14:01.697
It's about a transition from a kind of young adulthood post-collegiate life into just a more of an adult kind of sense of responsibility, sense of your place in the world.
它讲述的是从大学毕业后的那种年轻成年人生活，向更具责任感、更有成年人担当、对自己在世界上的位置有更清晰认知的阶段的转变。

00:14:01.697 --> 00:14:17.840
And, you know, James really models that for Barney, it's like, he's crossed over some like Rubicon that Barney was like, you know, it's this kind of, I was talking with a friend of mine last night and it's this great guy, Jamie, who I was friends with in my 20s, right?
而且，你知道，詹姆斯真的为巴尼做出了这种榜样，就像他跨过了一些巴尼觉得……你知道吗，我昨晚跟我一个朋友聊天，他是个超棒的家伙，叫杰米，是我二十多岁时的朋友，对吧？

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:28.582
And he's now, he just celebrated his 40th birthday, He's got two daughters and we were talking about how like when we were younger like youth was our brand It was our whole thing.
他现在刚庆祝完他的40岁生日，有两个女儿，我们当时就在聊，当年我们年轻的时候，青春就是我们的招牌，那是我们的全部。

00:14:28.582 --> 00:14:31.703
We were offering New York City was like we're young.
我们在纽约市打拼，就像是在说“我们还年轻”。

00:14:31.703 --> 00:14:46.766
We're here We're excited and then he was talking about a friend of his this woman who is bum She was like I didn't think aging would happen to me I thought that somehow that was like a mistake other people made was like by getting older It's a glitch.
我们来到了这里，非常兴奋，然后他谈到了他的一个朋友，这个女人挺沮丧的，她说：“我没想到衰老会发生在我身上，我以为那是别人身上才会犯的错”，就像变老是个程序漏洞一样。

00:14:46.766 --> 00:15:01.289
Yeah, and it's like we're not that won't happen to us and And there's, I don't know, there's just something like about the passage of time and you have to, in some ways, cooperate with it rather than fight against it, or it gets kind of ugly.
对，就好像我们——那不会发生在我们身上，而且，不知道为什么，时间流逝就是这样，你必须在某种程度上顺应它，而不是与它对抗，否则场面会变得有点难看。

00:15:01.289 --> 00:15:12.490
That's why I think shows like this are so successful, because you either have shows that are in the beginning stages, just like this is in terms of you graduate college and this much of life.
这就是为什么我认为像这样的剧会如此成功，因为你要么有那些处于人生起步阶段的剧，就像这部剧一样，讲的是你刚大学毕业，经历人生中这么大的一段。

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:20.019
And then you have successful shows that are about the other part of that journey, because it's coming and going.
然后你会有那些成功的剧，讲的是那段旅程的另一个部分，因为人生就是来来往往。

00:15:20.019 --> 00:15:33.740
And even now, you know, like as an adult, adult, adult with a 22-year-old kid and just that same thing that your friend was feeling is like, it surely couldn't happen to me.
甚至现在，你知道的，作为一个真正的大人、真正成年人，孩子都已经22岁了，你朋友当时感受到的那种心情也是一样的，就觉得这绝对不可能发生在我身上。

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:45.139
You feel that age and I think rather than fight against the machine, you have to go, oh, this is where I am now.
你能感受到那个年龄的增长，我觉得与其跟这股大趋势对抗，你不如接受：哦，这就是我现在的状态。

00:15:45.139 --> 00:15:47.820
And it's cool to watch journeys like that happen.
而且看着这样的旅程发生，其实挺酷的。

00:15:47.820 --> 00:16:03.539
And I don't think that I could appreciate my place either physically or work-wise or anything if it wasn't for cool experiences like how I met your mother, when you are younger, and you're feeling those things in that journey.
如果不是因为有像《老爸老妈浪漫史》这样精彩的经历——当你还年轻、在经历人生那段旅程并感受着这一切时——我是绝不会appreciate我现在无论是身体上还是工作上的位置，或者任何其他方面的。

00:16:03.539 --> 00:16:07.860
So the show is a microcosm because you're in one state when you're doing it.
所以这部剧是一个缩影，因为你在拍摄时正处于某一个人生阶段。

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:12.059
And then when you're older, looking back at you like, God, look at that guy.
然后当你变老了，回过头看当时的自己，会想：天哪，看看那个家伙。

00:16:12.059 --> 00:16:14.059
He had so much energy.
他当时精力真充沛啊。

00:16:14.059 --> 00:16:15.059
Yeah.
对。

00:16:15.059 --> 00:16:27.960
That's been one of the fun things for me and Craig is like the kind of the meta thing of like, we're older looking back on this time in our life and the narrator on the show is older looking back on this very particular time in his life.
对我跟克雷格来说，最有趣的事情之一就是这种元叙事的感觉，就是我们年纪大了，回头看我们人生中的这段时光，而剧中的旁白也是年纪大了，回头看他人生中这个非常特殊的时期。

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:34.819
So it allowed the making of the show allowed us this time capsule that we're now getting to dip back into and kind of reflect.
所以制作这部剧的过程给了我们这样一个时间胶囊，我们现在可以重新打开它，并进行某种反思。

00:16:34.819 --> 00:16:36.179
It's been really amazing.
这真的太奇妙了。

00:16:36.179 --> 00:16:45.620
I do want to say, I do find it so funny that high five thing like high fives are back because There's something about James and Barney.
我确实想说，我发现击掌这个梗太有趣了，击掌又流行回来了，因为詹姆斯和巴尼之间有一种奇妙的氛围。

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:48.580
They think they're dictating the terms of the culture.
他们觉得自己在引领文化潮流。

00:16:49.539 --> 00:16:51.500
Like, you know, he's got the blog.
就像，你知道的，他有博客。

00:16:51.779 --> 00:16:52.779
I'm bringing this back.
“我要把这个流行趋势带回来。”

00:16:52.779 --> 00:16:55.100
Like, it's like an all points bulletin.
这就像是一个全员通告。

00:16:55.100 --> 00:17:00.820
Like, it's on my shoulders to bring us back to the unwashed masses.
就好像把我们带回给那些乌合之众的重任，全扛在我肩膀上了。

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:01.460
Yes.
没错。

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:02.940
Yes.
是的。

00:17:02.940 --> 00:17:03.980
We're declaring it.
我们宣布了。

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:04.460
Yeah.
对。

00:17:04.579 --> 00:17:08.140
But it's very sweet how deferential Barney is to James.
但巴尼对詹姆斯的尊敬真的很贴心。

00:17:08.140 --> 00:17:09.259
Like, you're guys dynamic.
就像你们之间的化学反应。

00:17:09.259 --> 00:17:16.019
Like, I'm not surprised to hear that you and Neil had knew each other a little bit because you came in and you guys had a real chemistry there.
听到你和尼尔之前就认识一点，我一点也不惊讶，因为你一进来，你们之间就有一种真正的化学反应。

00:17:16.019 --> 00:17:17.019
And it's very cool.
这真的很酷。

00:17:17.019 --> 00:17:21.339
Barney is such a reprehensible character so much of the series.
在整部剧的大部分时间里，巴尼都是一个极其可恨的角色。

00:17:21.339 --> 00:17:23.180
He's out there doing terrible things.
他在外面做各种糟糕的事。

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:25.259
He's being a dick to women.
他对女性很混蛋。

00:17:25.259 --> 00:17:36.259
The moments we get to see his like vulnerability and how much he looks up to his big brother James and how much he clearly modeled his own personality on James.
但我们能看到他脆弱的一面，看到他多么崇拜他的大哥詹姆斯，以及他明显是以詹姆斯为模版来塑造自己的性格。

00:17:36.259 --> 00:17:46.920
It gives us like other dynamic very rarely on the show do you see Barney utterly in of somebody and the way he played that with you and then the place dramatically that it goes.
这展现了另一种动态，在这部剧中你很少看到巴尼对某个人彻底服气，他和你的对手戏把这一点表现得淋漓尽致，还有随之而来的戏剧性走向。

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:50.440
I'm wondering what that felt like doing that with him because he's in such armor so much of the time.
我很想知道和他演那样的戏是什么感觉，因为他大部分时间都把自己包裹在厚重的盔甲里。

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:53.240
He even says in this episode, like, what are our suits me and James?
他甚至在这集里说，我和詹姆斯的西装代表什么？

00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:55.000
It means we're a two man army.
这意味着我们是一支两人军队。

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:59.440
It's our armor, but his armor gets peeled away when he's around his big brother.
这是我们的盔甲，但当他在他大哥身边时，他的盔甲就被剥落了。

00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:07.359
That was really cool to see that dynamic with you guys and to see how raw and vulnerable Barney gets thinking he's losing his brother.
看到你们俩之间这种化学反应真的太酷了，看到巴尼在以为自己要失去哥哥时表现得那么真实、那么脆弱。

00:18:07.359 --> 00:18:09.680
You guys had real dramatic scenes in the end too.
你们最后也有非常具有戏剧性的戏份。

00:18:09.680 --> 00:18:14.240
Was it like kind of finding that chemistry of being his idol and then getting utterly lashed out at?
那种去找到既是他的偶像又被他狠狠大吼大叫的化学反应，是什么感觉？

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:15.839
He yells at James, right?
他对詹姆斯吼叫了，对吧？

00:18:15.839 --> 00:18:17.759
He, you guys have a very tense fight scene.
你们俩有一场非常紧张的争吵戏。

00:18:17.759 --> 00:18:18.759
What did it feel like?
当时感觉怎么样？

00:18:18.759 --> 00:18:19.680
I absolutely loved it.
我绝对爱极了。

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:42.880
It, yeah, because once again, it goes to the credit of the stories that you guys were telling and the way that you wrote it, that it was so rich to be able to, because there is a version of this script that is bad TV where James and Barney get together And they're basically doing the two wild and crazy guy sketch from SNL the whole time.
这——是的，因为再一次，这要归功于你们所讲述的故事以及你们的剧本创作方式，它是如此丰富，因为完全存在一种烂剧版本的剧本，就是詹姆斯和巴尼聚在一起，从头到尾基本上就像在演周六夜现场里的那两个疯狂搞笑的家伙。

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:43.880
Right.
没错。

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:44.920
And then there's never any growth.
然后就永远不会有任何成长。

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:57.119
The fact that James comes in kind of like that, then you find out that there's this twist that he has this whole thing is like, no, I'm settling down.
但事实是詹姆斯一开始也是那种形象，然后你会发现这里有个反转，他有这样一整套转变：不，我要安定下来了。

00:18:57.119 --> 00:18:59.200
I can't do that anymore.
我不能再那样做了。

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:09.519
And that Barney, who we've seen as this Helian, let's go of that armor and you see that hurt little kid, which then you're able to link to later.
巴尼在我们看来一直是那个坚强的人，他卸下了防备，让你看到了那个受伤的小孩，你之后也能把这些联系起来。

00:19:09.519 --> 00:19:13.079
Oh my God, like I know that we'll probably don't talk about that episode.
天哪，我知道我们可能不会谈论那一集。

00:19:13.079 --> 00:19:18.279
Oh, hopefully when it airs, but like with Ben, Ben later to have that complete arc.
哦，希望在播出的时候吧，但就像本一样，本后来有了那个完整的成长弧光。

00:19:18.279 --> 00:19:22.039
And this guy who's like, all I wanted was my dad.
这个家伙心里想的只有，我只想要我爸爸。

00:19:22.039 --> 00:19:23.440
All I wanted was my dad.
我只想要我爸爸。

00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:33.640
So then it, so then when that happened, I went, oh my God, in the beginning, we were basically setting up that I was kind of his dad figure too, because dad wasn't there.
所以当那件事发生时，我想，天哪，一开始，我们基本上就是在铺垫，我也算是他的父亲形象，因为父亲不在。

00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:38.839
So he had mom and mom had it locked down, but I was all he had in that regard.
所以他有妈妈，妈妈把一切都打理得井井有条，但在那方面我就是他的全部。

00:19:38.839 --> 00:19:40.880
So it just makes it so poignant.
所以这让人感到格外辛酸。

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:50.440
And to be able to have those moments in the midst of all these laughs, you can't ask for a better gift as an actor, really.
能够在这些欢笑声中展现出那些时刻，作为演员，你真的再也找不到比这更好的礼物了。

00:19:50.440 --> 00:20:02.359
I was gonna say, what I was struck by rewatching it, more than when we made it, I was struck by that all through that first half of that episode, before that big revelation comes out that James is engaged.
我是说，重看这一集时触动我的地方，甚至超过了我们拍摄的时候，让我感触深的是在这一集的前半部分，在詹姆斯订婚这个重磅消息揭晓之前。

00:20:02.359 --> 00:20:04.039
James is protecting Barney.
詹姆斯一直在保护巴尼。

00:20:04.039 --> 00:20:09.559
He's a little afraid of telling Barney the truth, but he knows it will crush Barney like a betrayal.
他有点害怕对巴尼说实话，但他知道这会像背叛一样击垮巴尼。

00:20:09.559 --> 00:20:19.400
So you're carrying this secret for like 60% of the episode and kind of putting on this front of being the big brother you know your little brother needs you to be.
所以你在大约60%的剧集里一直保守着这个秘密，表面上装作你弟弟所需要的那个好哥哥。

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:25.160
Clearly, biting your time to, at some point, tell him this huge life-changing piece of information.
显然是在等待时机，在某个时刻把这个重大的、改变人生轨迹的消息告诉他。

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:26.599
But I love the energy.
但我喜欢这种活力。

00:20:26.599 --> 00:20:35.059
You come in very hot and you're this super fun, whirling, dervish of energy, but you're holding onto the secret that you know is gonna come out.
你出场时气场十足，像个超级有趣、旋转不休的能量旋风，但你心里却藏着那个你知道迟早会曝光的秘密。

00:20:35.059 --> 00:20:36.420
And it's great, and it's great.
这真的很棒，真的很棒。

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:38.680
And once it comes out, everything changes.
一旦秘密揭晓，一切都变了。

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:45.339
And now it's like this drama for like the second half of the last third of the episode.
然后这就变成了后半段到最后三分之一的重头戏。

00:20:45.339 --> 00:20:47.460
I thought you played that all so beautifully.
我觉得你把这一切演得太精彩了。

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:49.380
You were sitting on that secret, you were amped up.
你一直憋着这个秘密，情绪处于亢奋状态。

00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:55.140
It came out, like all the beats were so well done, honestly, when it was so such a great performance.
秘密揭晓时，所有的节奏都把握得恰到好处，说实话，这真是一场绝佳的表演。

00:20:55.140 --> 00:21:04.319
It was such a cool layer to play because then at that point, point you've even think about it, even with us being in the club, that whole thing is an act.
这是一个非常酷的表演层次，因为在那之后，你甚至不用去想它，哪怕我们在俱乐部里，整场戏也全都是演出来的。

00:21:04.319 --> 00:21:18.700
And I think that we've all been to that point where, hey, man, yeah, we're doing this, but then I'm in the corner, talking to my guy, oh, no, no, I'm with you, I'm with you, having to carry that act up until you're like, look, man, I can't do this anymore.
我想我们都有过这样的经历，嘿，伙计，是的，我们正在这么做，但随后我走到角落里，跟我的哥们儿说，哦，不，不，我和你在一起，我和你在一起，不得不一直维持着这种伪装，直到你觉得，听着，伙计，我再也演不下去了。

00:21:18.700 --> 00:21:20.660
This is the truth.
这就是真相。

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:24.099
What a gift to be able to play that dichotomy.
能够演绎这种双重性真是一份厚礼。

00:21:24.099 --> 00:21:27.619
And in a sitcom, you don't get to do that in a sitcom a lot.
在情景喜剧中，你其实不常有机会这样做。

00:21:27.619 --> 00:21:32.220
I'm such a snob with the stuff that makes me laugh, which I feel we all should be.
我对能让我笑的东西要求很高，我觉得我们都应该这样。

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:36.420
So I love when you can have your cake and eat it, too.
所以我很喜欢鱼与熊掌兼得的时候。

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:38.299
And let me digress for a second.
请允许我扯开话题一会儿。

00:21:38.299 --> 00:21:39.299
Thank you.
谢谢。

00:21:39.299 --> 00:21:45.180
Do you know, maybe you don't know how well loved this show is across the world.
你知道吗，也许你并不知道这部剧在世界各地有多受欢迎。

00:21:45.180 --> 00:22:00.420
There were so many places that I go that depending on what you walk in the door with, they go, oh, yeah, that's Wayne from Who's Line of Love When You Do That or they like the gang show or they mention other sitcoms or they mention stage, there's like a lot to pull from.
我去过很多地方，根据你进门时受到的欢迎不同，他们会说，哦，对了，那是《谁是赢家》里的韦恩，当你在做那个的时候，或者他们喜欢这个帮派节目，或者他们提到其他情景喜剧，或者他们提到戏剧，有很多可以拿来聊的。

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:01.420
I'm very, very lucky.
我非常非常幸运。

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:02.420
Oh, man.
哦，天哪。

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:03.420
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:04.420
I love the Chappelle show shit.
我喜欢查佩尔秀的那种感觉。

00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:12.140
But there are people that I'll go get coffee just when at Mulan Rouge, there was this Brazilian tour group.
但有些人我去买咖啡时，正好在红磨坊，那里有一个巴西旅游团。

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:15.259
Half of the audience was this shout out Brazil.
半个观众都是这样，向巴西问好。

00:22:15.259 --> 00:22:17.220
They love how I met my brother.
他们喜欢《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

00:22:17.220 --> 00:22:18.220
Yeah.
是啊。

00:22:18.220 --> 00:22:19.220
I didn't know.
我当时不知道。

00:22:19.220 --> 00:22:21.940
was signing autographs outside afterwards.
散场后我在外面签名。

00:22:23.420 --> 00:22:28.420
Wayne, Wayne can barely speak English, but they love James.
韦恩，韦恩几乎不会说英语，但他们就是爱詹姆斯。

00:22:28.420 --> 00:22:30.420
How I had to bother you?
我怎么能打扰你呢？

00:22:30.420 --> 00:22:32.779
And in my mind, I was like, oh, that's very sweet.
而在我心里，我想，哦，这太甜了。

00:22:32.779 --> 00:22:35.740
I was like, I wasn't on the show that much to make an impact.
我想，我出场没那么多，产生不了太大影响。

00:22:35.740 --> 00:22:42.700
But then in talking to you, I remember the episodes and each time that I was dropped in, it was this little gift.
但后来和你交谈时，我想起了那些剧集，每一次我被安排登场，都是一份小礼物。

00:22:42.700 --> 00:22:44.099
So they were impactful episodes.
所以这些都是很有影响力的剧集。

00:22:44.099 --> 00:22:45.099
They were impactful.
它们很有影响力。

00:22:45.099 --> 00:22:47.140
So that's why I go, oh, yeah.
所以这就是为什么我会说，哦，对。

00:22:47.140 --> 00:22:51.579
I really was a part of something amazing that you guys built.
我真的成了你们所构建的惊人事物的一部分。

00:22:51.579 --> 00:22:53.019
So thank you for that.
所以为此谢谢你们。

00:22:53.019 --> 00:22:56.420
Oh my God, we were lucky to have you, man.
天哪，能有你加入真是我们的幸运，老兄。

00:22:56.420 --> 00:22:58.420
It's such a gift, we'd have had you on the show.
你能上我们的节目，真的是一份厚礼。

00:22:58.420 --> 00:23:04.619
It's wild to travel and you see the global reach of the thing.
到处旅行并看到这个节目的全球影响力，真的很疯狂。

00:23:04.619 --> 00:23:05.940
That's crazy for you.
对你来说这太疯狂了。

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:14.779
Yeah, yo, I mean, I got recognized at a Puja in India like a religious ceremony.
对啊，我是说，我在印度的神圣仪式上被认出来了。

00:23:14.779 --> 00:23:17.859
I got, I've been recognized in Africa and Tanzania.
我在非洲的坦桑尼亚也被认出来过。

00:23:17.859 --> 00:23:28.980
I mean, just wild, like, you know, you forget, it's so intimate, the filming of it, you forget that it's getting beamed all over the world and that it's life, it's so much longer.
我是说，真的很疯狂，你知道的，你会忘记，拍摄过程是那么的亲密，你忘了它正在向全世界播送，而且它的生命力是如此持久。

00:23:28.980 --> 00:23:35.380
And if you're lucky, which this show with this, we have been, you know, I wanted to just double back.
如果足够幸运的话——这部剧对我们来说确实如此，你知道的——我想折返回去聊聊。

00:23:35.380 --> 00:23:41.900
Like one of the things we talk about with Barney a lot is status and he's always trying to play high status.
就像我们经常讨论巴尼的一个方面是地位，他总是试图表现出高地位。

00:23:41.900 --> 00:23:44.859
It's like kind of part of his bit.
这有点像他的人设的一部分。

00:23:44.859 --> 00:23:49.140
But with you, you're higher status than him, you know?
但跟你在一起时，你的地位比他高，你知道吗？

00:23:49.140 --> 00:23:53.460
And I loved watching that kind of role reversal, like his deference to you.
我很喜欢看那种角色的反转，比如他对你的顺从和敬重。

00:23:53.460 --> 00:24:06.779
But it also, one of the things about aging, going out with the way that Barney goes out, the way that he wants to go out, the way he wants to make every single night, that this epic night, it's almost like a professional athlete.
但这也是关于变老的一点，以巴尼那种方式出门，以他想要的方式出门，他想把每一个夜晚都变成史诗般的夜晚，这几乎就像是个职业运动员。

00:24:06.779 --> 00:24:10.900
At some point, your body will be like, we're not doing, we can't do this anymore.
在某个时刻，你的身体会抗议说，我们不干了，我们再也受不了了。

00:24:10.900 --> 00:24:16.140
We literally don't have the single stamina, which is the name of the episode, right?
我们简直连单身汉的体力都没有了，这也是这一集的标题对吧？

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:18.539
Like we're tapped out, you know?
就像我们精疲力竭了一样，你知道吗？

00:24:18.539 --> 00:24:20.859
And I think in some ways there's a mercy to it.
而且我认为在某种程度上这也是一种解脱。

00:24:20.859 --> 00:24:27.140
Like, I don't know if you guys are like this, but when I was a kid, I could sleep till 1.130 in the afternoon.
就像，我不知道你们是不是这样，但当我还是个孩子的时候，我可以一直睡到下午一点半。

00:24:27.140 --> 00:24:30.619
My parents would be like, the day's done, the day you slept the day away, you know?
我父母会说，这一天都过完了，你把一天的时间都睡过去了，你知道吗？

00:24:30.619 --> 00:24:33.779
But at some point you just like, okay, I can't sleep past eight now.
但在某个时刻你会觉得，好吧，现在我八点以后就睡不着了。

00:24:33.779 --> 00:24:37.180
Okay, now I can't sleep past 7.15, what's going on?
好吧，现在我七点十五分以后就睡不着了，这是怎么回事？

00:24:37.180 --> 00:24:42.539
And I think again, like with rolling with it, I actually discovered that the mornings were pretty terrific.
我想同样地，随着年龄的增长顺其自然，我实际上发现早晨的时光非常棒。

00:24:42.539 --> 00:24:45.700
I never knew mornings, because unless I had an early class, I can call it.
我从来不知道什么是早晨，除非我有早课，否则我完全起不来。

00:24:45.700 --> 00:24:48.539
I just was like, oh, mornings are great.
我当时就觉得，哦，早晨真棒。

00:24:48.539 --> 00:24:54.259
So I think like, you kind of have to cooperate with nature a little bit and be like, okay, things are shifting, you know?
所以我觉得，你多少得顺应一下自然，然后想，好吧，情况正在发生变化，你知道吗？

00:24:54.259 --> 00:24:56.619
And I think that's what James is like, he's going with it.
而且我认为詹姆斯就是这样，他在顺应这种变化。

00:24:56.619 --> 00:25:02.059
He's like, this is, you know, it's not just his heart, it's his body is also telling him to slow down.
他就像是，你知道的，不仅仅是他的心，他的身体也在告诉他要放慢脚步。

00:25:02.059 --> 00:25:06.730
Because if he's been an athlete of the club games, Right.
因为如果他一直都是俱乐部比赛的运动员，没错。

00:25:06.730 --> 00:25:10.418
Then, then at some point, your knees give up.
那么，到了某个时候，你的膝盖就会撑不住。

00:25:10.418 --> 00:25:12.221
Man, my knees gave up.
老天，我的膝盖已经撑不住了。

00:25:12.221 --> 00:25:15.007
I've already got five, five rings.
我已经有五个，五个戒指了。

00:25:15.007 --> 00:25:15.507
Yes.
是的。

00:25:15.507 --> 00:25:16.982
The MVP last year.
去年的MVP。

00:25:16.982 --> 00:25:17.482
Yeah.
是的。

00:25:17.482 --> 00:25:19.039
I think we need to.
我想我们需要。

00:25:19.039 --> 00:25:20.842
Nothing left to prove.
没有什么需要再证明的了。

00:25:20.579 --> 00:25:27.220
I've gotten to a point where, and, and this happened about 10 years ago, I can be in a club.
我已经到了这样一个阶段——大约在10年前发生的——我可以在夜店里。

00:25:27.220 --> 00:25:29.756
If someone goes, Hey, let's go out.
如果有人说，嘿，我们出去玩吧。

00:25:29.756 --> 00:25:30.256
Sure.
当然。

00:25:30.256 --> 00:25:33.517
The whole nine, I can sit right there and go.
各种流程全套下来，我可以直接坐在那儿然后。

00:25:33.380 --> 00:25:35.562
Wayne has fallen asleep for those.
