真是恰到好处又极其有趣，你看起来——你看起来完全不像那种脑子里正经历着疯狂自我怀疑的人，听到你也有那种声音让我感到无比欣慰，因为你刚刚走进来的时候，那种状态简直就像是毫不费力地把这种情绪实体化了。你在自我批判两秒钟后还能来这里，我觉得把这一点分享给观众简直是一种公益行为，但我认为这就是剧场演员的特质，我认为这就是剧场演员的特质，因为剧场演员就是会把自己纵身扔下桥，然后完全相信蹦极绳会接住他。你知道的，就像是，对，对，因为你必须得——我一直都能听到那种声音，甚至当我教课时我都会说，听着，这就是我所听到的。

00:34:06.859 --> 00:34:17.280
It's always, but I've trained myself so much that, that you will not see that on the outside, but I'm hearing that screaming.
总是这样，但我已经训练了自己很久，所以你在外表上绝对看不出来，但我其实能听到那个尖叫的声音。

00:34:17.519 --> 00:34:22.679
And so I get to a point where like, well, I'm here, I'm in costume now.
所以我会到达这样一个状态：好吧，我在这里，我现在穿着戏服呢。

00:34:22.679 --> 00:34:26.239
Oh, there's an audience, or there's cameras.
哦，台下有观众，或者有摄像机。

00:34:26.239 --> 00:34:28.079
You can't stop now.
你现在可不能停下来。

00:34:28.079 --> 00:34:33.880
The time to stop would have been when you got the phone call weeks ago, and when you, so you're here now.
真正该停下来的时机，应该是在几周前你接到电话的时候，或者是当你决定来的时候，所以你现在已经在这里了。

00:34:33.880 --> 00:34:41.920
So that's my way of, and then once you jump and the bungee, then it's the most exhilarating feeling in the world.
所以这就是我的应对方式，一旦你跳下去并且绳索发挥了作用，那就会变成世界上最让人肾上腺素飙升的感觉。

00:34:41.920 --> 00:34:43.519
And so doing that was great.
所以这样做感觉太棒了。

00:34:43.519 --> 00:34:48.440
Yeah, but I agree, you have to travel through the valley of fear and panic.
对，但我同意，你必须得穿过恐惧和恐慌的山谷。

00:34:48.440 --> 00:34:51.159
I've never figured out a way to not do that.
我从来没找到过能不经历这个过程的方法。

00:34:51.159 --> 00:34:56.320
And in fact, sometimes I think there's a way to be almost too relaxed where you're not gonna do your best work.
事实上，有时我认为如果表现得太放松，反而做不出最好的作品。

00:34:56.320 --> 00:35:02.960
Like, there's a point of like tension and readiness that is almost athletic, right?
就像，有一种紧张感和准备状态，几乎可以说是运动级别的，对吧？

00:35:02.960 --> 00:35:09.039
Like it's like before a game, like you wanna be loose, but you wanna be like, just at the edge, you know, put me out there.
就像比赛前一样，你既想保持放松，但又必须处于那种箭在弦上的边缘状态，你知道的，把我派上场吧。

00:35:09.039 --> 00:35:10.860
You can't fool an audience.
你是骗不过观众的。

00:35:10.860 --> 00:35:19.800
Some people can fool them just enough, but I truly believe this after decades of doing this on stage, even night lead, now when I'm doing this show or when I'm touring.
有些人或许能勉强糊弄过去，但我深信不疑——在舞台上经历了数十年之后，甚至现在每晚如此，无论是我做这个节目还是在巡演时。

00:35:19.800 --> 00:35:23.239
If you, I love the use of tension.
如果你——我喜欢那种紧张感的运用。

00:35:23.239 --> 00:35:31.400
If the audience senses that you're there and you're prowling like a cat and you're ready to do your thing and you jump into whatever it is, they're there with you.
如果观众感觉到你在那里，像猫一样在暗中盘桓，随时准备好大展身手，并且全身心投入到接下来的表演中，他们就会一直跟你在一起。

00:35:31.400 --> 00:35:37.599
And just like when they're watching you on screen, they can feel the way that an edit made the scene build in the performances.
就像他们在屏幕上看着你一样，他们能感受到剪辑如何让场景和表演逐渐推向高潮。

00:35:37.599 --> 00:35:43.760
If you come out, you're like, oh man, I just did Kansas City City last night and I'm home, this is a cakewalk.
如果你出场时表现得像是：“哦天哪，我昨晚刚演完堪萨斯城，现在回到主场，这简直轻而易举。”

00:35:43.760 --> 00:35:47.719
As soon as you come out, laissez-faire, they know it.
你一出来带着这种漫不经心的态度，他们一眼就能看穿。

00:35:47.719 --> 00:35:49.000
Maybe they'll laugh.
也许他们还是会笑。

00:35:49.000 --> 00:35:51.199
They'll still be with you, but there's something missing.
他们依然会支持你，但就是有什么东西缺失了。

00:35:51.199 --> 00:36:00.800
And I promised myself that years ago, I said, I would rather not do the thing I'm doing at that second than go out there and not feel that even on camera.
我多年前就向自己保证过，我说，我宁愿不做当下正在做的那件事，也绝不在登台时没有那种感觉，哪怕是在镜头前也是如此。

00:36:00.800 --> 00:36:02.880
You have to show up because it's in your eyes.
你必须全力以赴，因为这一切都写在你的眼神里。

00:36:02.880 --> 00:36:04.880
Yeah, I just hear what it sounds like.
对，我只是听听它听起来是什么样。

00:36:04.880 --> 00:36:10.039
What I hear you describing is like being a professional, like just being a pro, you know what I mean?
我听你描述的这种感觉就像是做一个专业人士，也就是纯粹的专业，你知道我的意思吗？

00:36:10.039 --> 00:36:15.000
And no one sustains a career as long as yours without being an absolute pro.
而且没有人能在没有绝对专业精神的情况下，维持像你这么长的职业生涯。

00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:25.320
But what people don't understand is that your level of talent and accomplishment has nothing to do with whether or not you're gonna vomit in the stall before you go out there.
但人们不明白的是，你的天赋和成就达到了什么水平，跟你在上台前会不会在隔间里呕吐其实毫无关系。

00:36:25.320 --> 00:36:32.000
Like Maria Callis, like the greatest opera singer of the 20th century, apparently vomited before every performance from nerves.
就像玛丽亚·卡拉斯，20世纪最伟大的歌剧演员，据说每次演出前都会因为紧张而呕吐。

00:36:32.000 --> 00:36:43.800
You know, there are people that just can, yeah, it's like, I think that in some ways, your level of fear is commensurate with how much you care in a lot of ways, you know.
你知道的，有些人就是能——对，我觉得在某种程度上，你的恐惧程度往往与你在乎的程度成正比，你知道的。

00:36:43.800 --> 00:36:44.381
do that.
我就这样。

00:36:44.381 --> 00:36:47.145
I do that before every podcast record.
我每次录播客前都这样。

00:36:47.145 --> 00:36:49.545
Sorry, I don't look so good away.
抱歉，我看起来状态不太好。

00:36:49.545 --> 00:36:52.163
I was very nervous to see you today.
我今天见到你时非常紧张。

00:36:52.163 --> 00:36:54.199
Just being around the gills.
整个人都有点不自在。

00:36:54.199 --> 00:36:54.699
Yeah.
对。

00:36:54.699 --> 00:36:56.827
Do you know another moment I loved?
你知道我喜欢的另一个桥段是什么吗？

00:36:56.827 --> 00:37:00.474
I love the dramatic stuff at the end between you and Barney.
我喜欢你和巴尼在最后的那场情感冲突。

00:37:00.474 --> 00:37:02.055
I love the fight you have.
我喜欢你们之间的争吵。

00:37:02.055 --> 00:37:09.836
I love the way when they reconcile, when you reveal, first of all, Neil's turned the moment he hears there's going to be a baby.
我喜欢你们重修旧好的方式，尤其是当你透露——首先，尼尔一听到有孩子要出生，整个人态度立刻就变了。

00:37:09.639 --> 00:37:12.280
It's one of my favorite Neil moments in the show, I think.
我觉得这是尼尔在这部剧中最棒的时刻之一。

00:37:12.280 --> 00:37:14.079
Babies are Barney's Kryptonite.
孩子就是巴尼的氪石。

00:37:14.079 --> 00:37:14.920
It's true.
确实如此。

00:37:14.920 --> 00:37:18.280
That's true in the finale of the whole series, but we'll get there at some point.
这在整部剧的大结局中确实如此，但我们总会聊到那里的。

00:37:18.280 --> 00:37:21.360
But like babies are Barney's vulnerability.
不过像小婴儿这种东西，就是巴尼的软肋。

00:37:21.360 --> 00:37:23.639
That made my wife laughed so hard.
那让我妻子笑得前俯后仰。

00:37:23.639 --> 00:37:24.679
There's gonna be a baby.
将要有一个宝宝了。

00:37:24.679 --> 00:37:27.039
I was really moved by it too.
我也真的深受触动。

00:37:27.039 --> 00:37:34.840
I was like my eyes weld up in that scene because Barney's just so broken and he just wants to be important to his brother.
当时那场戏我的眼眶都湿润了，因为巴尼实在是太崩溃了，他只是想在他哥哥心里占据重要位置。

00:37:34.840 --> 00:37:40.599
He thinks he's gonna lose his brother who's kind of like we said, his father too in some ways, his older brother's kind of his father.
他觉得自己快要失去哥哥了——就像我们刚才说的，在某种程度上这也是他的父亲，他大哥哥某种程度上就像是父亲。

00:37:40.599 --> 00:37:46.440
And the moment he hears that he's going to gain family, he's going to gain a new role of being Uncle Barney.
而当他听说自己将要拥有家人、将要获得“巴尼叔叔”这个新身份时。

00:37:46.440 --> 00:37:48.800
And it's funny because the future narrator always refers to Uncle Barney.
有趣的是，未来的旁白总是提到“巴尼叔叔”。

00:37:48.800 --> 00:37:50.119
Like that was his nickname in the group.
就好像那是他在朋友圈里的外号一样。

00:37:50.119 --> 00:37:53.719
No, this is the moment he actually becomes Uncle Barney.
不，这才是他真正变成巴尼叔叔的时刻。

00:37:53.719 --> 00:37:56.199
And it's like his greatest honor of his life.
这就像是他一生中最大的荣誉。

00:37:56.199 --> 00:37:57.760
And he says, I'm going to be an uncle.
他说：“我要当叔叔了。”

00:37:57.760 --> 00:38:02.960
And the way James says to him, the way you play it at when was for the rest of your life.
而詹姆斯对他说的那句，你当时的表现是“为了你的余生”。

00:38:02.960 --> 00:38:07.239
And you say it to him in this way that is like so lovely and such a gift to him.
你对他说的那种方式是如此可爱，简直是送给他的一份大礼。

00:38:07.239 --> 00:38:08.320
And he's about to cry.
他快要哭了。

00:38:08.320 --> 00:38:18.239
I was watching it yesterday before knowing we're going to talk and I started to cry this great like replacement song that would the sky way by this awesome band the replacement starts to play.
昨天在我们准备录节目之前我还在看，看着看着我就哭了起来，那个超级棒的乐队The Replacements的一首很赞的插曲《Skyway》开始播放。

00:38:18.239 --> 00:38:23.079
It is such a beautiful moment that takes us into that flash forward a year later.
这是一个绝美的时刻，把我们带入了一年后的闪回。

00:38:23.079 --> 00:38:25.960
We hint at where our characters are a year later.
我们暗示了角色们一年后的去向。

00:38:25.960 --> 00:38:29.960
We say Marshall and Willie have gotten married in that year, which is a huge reveal.
我们提到马歇尔和莉莉在那一年里已经结婚了，这是一个巨大的反转。

00:38:29.960 --> 00:38:32.559
You're not sure what Ted and Robin status is.
你不确定泰德和罗宾的状态是什么。

00:38:32.559 --> 00:38:36.400
Robin and Ted, there's a little hint of neither of them are tired.
罗宾和泰德，有一个小小的暗示，他们俩都不累。

00:38:36.400 --> 00:38:37.400
Why are they not tired?
为什么他们不累？

00:38:37.400 --> 00:38:39.760
Why do they seem to have single stamina a year later?
为什么一年后他们好像还保持着单身的精力？

00:38:39.760 --> 00:38:41.519
Robin and Ted, are they now not together?
罗宾和泰德，他们现在难道没有在一起吗？

00:38:41.519 --> 00:38:45.760
And that was like a little hint, little bread crumb for the audience to think about.
这就像是一个小小的暗示、留给观众去思考的面包屑。

00:38:45.760 --> 00:38:57.840
But that, the warmth of Barney being an uncle to this little baby and like James giving him the ultimate gift of here is more, we didn't have, we didn't get to have a dad growing up but I've given you a nephew.
但是，巴尼作为这个小宝宝的叔叔所展现出的那种温暖，以及詹姆斯送给他的终极礼物——这里还有更多，我们从小没有爸爸，但我给你带来了个外甥。

00:38:57.840 --> 00:38:59.360
It's, I was so moved by it.
这真的让我太感动了。

00:38:59.360 --> 00:39:01.039
It was a really beautiful ending.
这是一个非常美好的结局。

00:39:01.039 --> 00:39:13.320
Him being an uncle and loving babies, just like in the finale, like you said, I really feel that it is also because of his, it's his, his, his origin story.
他当了叔叔而且喜欢婴儿，就像在大结局里那样，正如你所说，我真的觉得这也是因为他的……这是他的出身背景。

00:39:13.320 --> 00:39:23.159
Growing up, James was his guy, always seeking dad, reading those letters or talking about, you know, oh, dad is this and dad's doing that.
从小到大，詹姆斯就是他的精神支柱，总是渴望父亲，读那些信，或者谈论，你知道的，哦，爸爸是这样的，爸爸在做那个。

00:39:23.159 --> 00:39:34.599
That it's just natural that this guy would turn around and if, and parent and want to parent that child or be able to protect that child.
所以这个家伙回过头来，如果去抚养或者想要抚养那个孩子，或者能够保护那个孩子，这是再自然不过的事情了。

00:39:34.599 --> 00:39:38.780
because we all want to protect the little child that we can protect.
因为我们都想保护那个我们可以保护的小孩。

00:39:38.780 --> 00:39:40.239
Absolutely it's that.
绝对就是这样。

00:39:40.239 --> 00:39:42.320
Yeah, yeah, so true.
对啊，对啊，太对了。

00:39:42.320 --> 00:39:47.400
And also I think James is doing some very good fathering of Barney in that moment.
而且我也觉得詹姆斯在那一刻对巴尼起到了很好的父亲般的引导作用。

00:39:47.400 --> 00:39:52.039
Like he's actually stepping forward and going, it's time for all of us to grow up.
就像他实际上站出来说：“我们所有人都该长大了。”

00:39:52.039 --> 00:40:06.639
I think sometimes when men are like, don't have a kind of role model, it doesn't have to be a father, it could be any sort of like strong male role model, they'll seek what it means to be a man from all sorts of like insane ideas, you know?
我觉得有时候当男人们没有某种榜样时——不一定非得是父亲，可以是任何那种强大的男性榜样——他们会从各种疯狂的想法中去寻找“男子汉”究竟意味着什么，你知道吗？

00:40:06.639 --> 00:40:14.119
They'll cobble it together from like all sorts of disparate sources that might not be the best kind of game plan, right?
他们会从各种大相径庭的渠道东拼西凑出答案，而那可能并不是最好的行动方针，对吧？

00:40:14.119 --> 00:40:21.599
And, you know, part of a kind of side plot of this whole show is watching Barney like learn.
而且，你知道，这部剧整体的一个副线剧情就是看巴尼如何学习成长。

00:40:21.599 --> 00:40:33.599
It's really watching a bunch of people grow into their, you know, like assuming like growing out of their boy or their girl and into their adult persona, you know?
这其实就是看一群人慢慢长大，你知道的，比如摆脱他们的男孩或女孩心态，蜕变成他们成人的模样，你知道吗？

00:40:33.599 --> 00:40:36.099
Yeah, we're all adolescents to like 30, basically.
对，我们基本上到30岁都还是青少年。

00:40:36.099 --> 00:40:37.599
It is the premise of the show.
这就是本剧的前提。

00:40:37.599 --> 00:40:38.599
Absolutely.
完全正确。

00:40:38.599 --> 00:40:42.480
Hey, Craig, it was, that was the voice of Megan Mulally, right?
嘿，克雷格，那是梅根·莫拉莉的声音对吧？

00:40:42.480 --> 00:40:43.320
Doing the...
就是那个……

00:40:43.320 --> 00:40:46.239
I was just gonna say, is everyone, does everyone know that trivia, fun fact?
我正想说，大家知道不知道这个冷知识、趣事？

00:40:46.239 --> 00:40:51.239
The voice, you know, the Charlie Brown's parents, like, you know, you don't see her face, you don't see Barney and James' mom's face.
那个声音，你知道的，就像查理·布朗的父母那样，你看不到她的脸，你看不到巴尼和詹姆斯妈妈的脸。

00:40:51.239 --> 00:40:53.039
That's Megan Mulally's voice.
那是梅根·莫拉莉的声音。

00:40:53.039 --> 00:40:54.679
And it was uncredited, I think, at the time.
而且当时好像是没有署名的。

00:40:54.679 --> 00:40:58.960
I think that only came out later because she was just like a friend of the show and she was like, yeah, I'll do that.
我想后来才曝光的，因为她只是剧组的一个朋友，然后她就说，好吧，我来录那个。

00:40:58.960 --> 00:41:02.320
Well, she, Megan had, remember she had a talk show at that time.
哦，梅根当时，记得她那时候有个脱口秀节目吗？

00:41:02.320 --> 00:41:03.159
A talk show.
一个脱口秀节目。

00:41:03.159 --> 00:41:06.719
Very first talk show appearance was on Meghan Mulally.
我第一次上脱口秀就是在梅根·莫拉莉的节目。

00:41:06.719 --> 00:41:12.880
She was so lovely and Nick Offerman, her husband, was hanging around on set and was so nice to me.
她人超级好，她的丈夫尼克·奥弗曼当时也在片场闲逛，对我也非常好。

00:41:12.880 --> 00:41:16.400
And that was before he was on Parks and Rec or anything.
那还是他在出演《公园与游憩》或其他作品之前。

00:41:16.400 --> 00:41:19.880
And I've always loved the two of them because they were so good.
我一直都很喜欢他们俩，因为他们太优秀了。

00:41:19.880 --> 00:41:24.659
But then I think our first all cast appearance was on the Meghan Mulally show.
但后来我想我们全剧组第一次公开亮相就是在梅根·莫拉莉的节目上。

00:41:24.659 --> 00:41:26.480
She invited all of us on.
她邀请了我们所有人去。

00:41:26.480 --> 00:41:28.960
So she was already a bit of a friend of the show.
所以她当时就已经算是剧组的朋友了。

00:41:28.960 --> 00:41:31.000
I feel like she did it during that appearance.
我觉得她就是在那次亮相期间录的。

00:41:31.000 --> 00:41:33.199
I feel like you guys went there and she banged out that line.
我觉得是你们去上节目的时候，她顺便就把那句台词给录了。

00:41:33.199 --> 00:41:36.360
Those few lines for us as Barney James, this one.
为我们饰演巴尼和詹姆斯的妈妈录了那几句台词。

00:41:36.360 --> 00:41:47.840
Hey, when Barney throws the phone at you and you have that like complicated like juggling of the phone, was that, I can't remember, is that planned or was that something that just happened?
嘿，当巴尼把电话扔给你，而你来了一段那种复杂的抛接电话时，我记不清了，那是排练好的还是纯属巧合？

00:41:47.840 --> 00:41:50.599
Like remember you, the phone like you.
就像记得你，那电话就像你……

00:41:50.599 --> 00:41:53.679
There's like a hot potato phone moment that was very impressively done.
有一个击鼓传花式的接电话动作，完成得非常帅气。

00:41:53.679 --> 00:41:58.880
